more likely we'll see isps do deals like NTL did
use bt as a VOD delivery method
for &quot;legit&quot; content only
then caches won't have the desired effect, since much of the traffic is caused by illegal content...
nobody wants to get their hands anywhere near illegal content
bsuiness wise
see limewire got sued?
well, iirc the JPC caching method was content-agnostic and from what you've told me the cachelogic one isn't...
yeah, i know
but it might be easier to test things like that in a less stringent jurisdiction where ISPs still have problems with BT traffic
maybe canada? ^^
it's not so much that content can or cannot be obvisously identified
it's that they &quot;know&quot; most of it will be illegal
and dont want to be sued
i see :/
they are legally OK now, even if it does cost them hundreds of K (or millions) of $ in bandwidth
small potatoes compared to the court cases and settlements these days
it's all a big crazy mess
